into a terminal three to four times a day.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;So, after Jane Street&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a href="https://blog.janestreet.com/can-you-reverse-engineer-an-asic/"&gt;gauntlet&lt;/a&gt; turned up in my feed for the third time since August, I decided to type &lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;continue&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt; at them.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://www.babush.me/images/jane-asic/chip-hero.png" alt="The puzzle die: the whole 200 x 353 um layout, and a detail of the standard-cell rows" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full disclosure:&lt;/strong&gt; my attempt is past the challenge deadline, and people have published writeups since then. Make of that what you will.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>